                "content": "To calculate the average value (mean) of a variable from the mtcars data set, find the sum of all values, and divide the sum by the number of values.\n\nSorted observation of wt (weight)\n\n 1.513\n 1.615\n 1.835\n 1.935\n 2.140\n 2.200\n 2.320\n 2.465\n\n 2.620\n 2.770\n 2.780\n 2.875\n 3.150\n 3.170\n 3.190\n 3.215\n\n 3.435\n 3.440\n 3.440\n 3.440\n 3.460\n 3.520\n 3.570\n 3.570\n\n 3.730\n 3.780\n 3.840\n 3.845\n 4.070\n 5.250\n 5.345\n 5.424\n\nLuckily for us, the mean() function in R can do it for you:\n\nExample\nFind the average weight (wt) of a car:\n\n Data_Cars <- mtcars\n\nmean(Data_Cars$wt)\n\nResult:\n\n[1] 3.21725\n\nTry it Yourself »",
